CLAUDE:
Glad that did it! A sneaky bug — leading spaces in URLs are invisible but completely break 
the connection. Good one to remember for the future.
 
The original configuration had:
    os.environ['HANDS_ON_AI_SERVER'] = ' https://ollama.locollm.org'
                                        ^ space here was the problem
 
The fix was simply:
    os.environ['HANDS_ON_AI_SERVER'] = 'https://ollama.locollm.org'
 
This is a common real-world debugging scenario — the error message pointed to a connection 
problem but the actual cause was invisible whitespace in the URL string. This demonstrates 
the importance of careful string handling in configuration code.
